=== concentrated_strike_after_letters
The next three days are consumed with work. She organizes makeshift medical stations, though many herbs and supplies were lost in the fires. 

Able-bodied troops help villagers replant fields and rebuild food storage, though famine looms like a shadow. 

Every day, she battles with guilt, weighing whether to cut down the troops’ rations to feed the villagers. 

Her soldiers look to her for strength, and she cannot afford to leave them weakened, yet each hungry face she sees among the villagers twists the knife deeper. She balances it as best she can.

When the new captain arrives with reinforcements and word that aid will follow, she leaves. As she mounts her steed, the weight of her summons presses heavily on her shoulders. 

Behind her, she leaves scorched fields, hollow eyes, and a hunger that will outlast her presence. Ahead lies the capital, the Palace.

-> soldier_chapter2_concentrated_strike